cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PyroWISE — wildfire-spread simulation engine"
message: "If you use PyroWISE or build on its open scientific documentation, please cite it as follows."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Infordata Sistemi Srl Società Benefit"
    city: "Trieste"
    country: "IT"
    website: "https://infordata.it"
repository-code: "https://github.com/infordata-sistemi/pyrowise"
url: "https://github.com/infordata-sistemi/pyrowise"
abstract: >
  PyroWISE is a wildfire-spread simulation engine implementing the Canadian
  Forest Fire Danger Rating System science stack — the Fire Weather Index
  System (Van Wagner, 1987) and the Fire Behavior Prediction System
  (Forestry Canada Fire Danger Group, 1992) — with elliptical Huygens
  wavefront perimeter propagation (Richards, 1990; Anderson et al., 1982;
  Tymstra et al., 2010) and a quasi-static eikonal arrival-time kernel. A
  Rothermel/FBFM40 spread provider (Rothermel, 1972; Scott & Burgan, 2005)
  is available behind the same interface for cross-comparison with US
  engines. Calibrated for the cross-border Karst region of Italy and
  Slovenia, it is the simulation core of the TerraWise
  territorial-emergency platform and the Karst Firewall 5.0 EU Interreg
  project (ITA-SI0600146, 2024–2027).
keywords:
  - wildfire
  - fire-spread simulation
  - CFFDRS
  - FWI
  - FBP
  - Huygens propagation
  - Rothermel
  - digital twin
  - Karst
  - Interreg
  - TerraWise
